# ---------------------------------------------------------------- derived art
#
# The photographs (src/assets/<year>/*.webp, cut by tools/photos.mjs from the
# camera masters beside them) and the hero loop with its poster frame
# (src/assets/hero-loop.webm and hero-still.webp, rendered by
# tools/hero-loop.mjs from src/scene/synthwave.js) are all produced by scripts
# and never edited by hand -- but they are TRACKED anyway, and deliberately.
#
# The deploy builds from a fresh clone and runs nothing but `vite build`, and
# the components import these files by name, so a clone without them does not
# build. Committing ~2MB of art is the cheap half of that trade; the expensive
# half is making every deploy re-render the loop through a native canvas and
# an ffmpeg binary. If you re-run either script, commit what it wrote.
#
# src/assets/wave.webp has no script and no master in the tree -- it arrived as
# a lossless WebP that was compressed once, by hand, and the original is only
# in the first commit. That makes it a source file, not an artifact.
